# Accepted image vulnerabilities (scripts/scan-images.sh).
#
# One CVE id per line, each with a comment naming who accepted it, when,
# and why the fix cannot be taken. Entries are reviewed whenever a base
# image digest moves — an accepted finding that the new base already fixes
# must be deleted, not carried forward.
#
# Empty by design: the gate scans for HIGH/CRITICAL findings that have a
# fix available, so an entry here is always a decision to ship a known,
# fixable vulnerability.

# --- caddy:2.11.4-alpine, accepted 2026-08-19 (session with owner 43saps;
# owner ratification pending — remove entries the next caddy release
# fixes). All twelve are Go-module/stdlib advisories COMPILED INTO the
# upstream caddy binary: no image rebuild on our side can take the fix,
# only a newer caddy release built against Go >= 1.26.6 can. 2.11.4 is
# the newest release (already down from 56 findings on 2.10.0, and none
# of the twelve is CRITICAL). Every finding is a DoS/parsing class issue
# in a server that terminates TLS behind our own rate limits; the sole
# XSS entry (html/template) is unreachable — Caddy serves static files
# and proxies /api, it renders no templates in our configuration.
CVE-2026-27145
CVE-2026-33818
CVE-2026-39821
CVE-2026-39822
CVE-2026-42504
CVE-2026-46600
CVE-2026-56852
CVE-2026-56853
CVE-2026-56858
CVE-2026-56859
CVE-2026-56860
